                        "field":  "rule",
                        "proposed":  "SPECIAL-LAW:this-section exclusively governs every current-and-future directory+registry+catalog+index-of-authoritative-identities; OWNER:permission-sovereign solely owns directory definition+schema+identity+registration+classification+relationship+version+activation+retirement+read-scope+write-decision+supervision; EXECUTION:governed-executor only after exact permission-sovereign decision; STORAGE:decision-sovereign manages data integrity and storage modules without directory-content authority; DOMAIN-OWNERS:may submit candidates+read authorized projections+own referenced domain bodies but cannot create+rename+mutate+activate+retire directory entries; PRECEDENCE:this-special-law prevails over general provisions for directory matters; CONSOLIDATION:A5+C8+A55-B41 and every future directory provision inherit this ownership automatically; ENTRY:all directory access through permission-directory official entry or its explicitly registered typed subdirectory route; FAILURE:directory unavailable or inconsistent=\u003eaffected authorization fails-closed while unrelated runtime individuals remain available under B24 DIRECTORY-STORAGE:every directory managed by permission-core is persisted in the registered local PostgreSQL authority only; PostgreSQL is the sole current structured storage and transaction boundary for directory entries,relationships,lifecycle and write receipts; alternate embedded database,file,cache,mirror or module-private state cannot be directory authority or write fallback."
